{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Application to security for residential rental agreements","requirement":"Section applies to security for a rental agreement for residential property used as the tenant's dwelling.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["residential property used as tenant's dwelling","security for rental agreement"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(a)","quoted_span":"This section applies to security for a rental agreement for residential property that is used as the dwelling of the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Definition of security","requirement":"“Security” includes any payment, fee, deposit, or charge imposed at the beginning of the tenancy to reimburse the landlord for new-tenant processing costs or as advance rent, and may be used for rent default, damages beyond ordinary wear and tear, cleaning, and returning personal property or appurtenances.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["imposed at beginning of tenancy","processing new tenant or advance rent","used for specified purposes"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["Section 1950.6"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(b)","quoted_span":"“security” means any payment, fee, deposit, or charge, including, but not limited to, any payment, fee, deposit, or charge, except as provided in Section 1950.6, that is imposed at the beginning of the tenancy to be used to reimburse the landlord for costs associated with processing a new tenant or that is imposed as an advance payment of rent","interaction":null,"confidence":0.96,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"One month's rent security limit","requirement":"Except for paragraphs (2), (3), or (5), a landlord shall not demand or receive security exceeding one month's rent, in addition to first month's rent paid on or before initial occupancy.","key_value":{"max_security":"one month's rent","additional_allowed":"first month's rent paid on or before initial occupancy"},"coverage_conditions":["residential rental agreement","security however denominated"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["advance payment of at least six months' rent if lease term is six months or longer","mutual agreement for tenant-requested alterations for fee","small landlord two-month cap under (c)(5)"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(1)","quoted_span":"a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to one month’s rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy.","interaction":"Subject to exceptions in (c)(2), (c)(3), and (c)(5).","confidence":0.99,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Six-month advance rent exception","requirement":"The one-month security limit does not prohibit an advance payment of not less than six months' rent if the lease term is six months or longer.","key_value":{"advance_rent_min":"six months' rent","lease_term_min":"six months"},"coverage_conditions":["lease term six months or longer"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(2)","quoted_span":"This subdivision does not prohibit an advance payment of not less than six months’ rent if the term of the lease is six months or longer.","interaction":"Exception to (c)(1).","confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant-requested alteration agreement exception","requirement":"The one-month security limit does not preclude a landlord and tenant from mutually agreeing, at the tenant's request and for a specified fee, to make structural, decorative, furnishing, or similar alterations other than cleaning or repairing chargeable to prior tenant under subdivision (e).","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["mutual agreement","tenant request","specified fee or charge","alterations other than cleaning/repair"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(3)","quoted_span":"This subdivision does not preclude a landlord and a tenant from entering into a mutual agreement for the landlord, at the request of the tenant and for a specified fee or charge, to make structural, decorative, furnishing, or other similar alterations","interaction":"Exception to (c)(1).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Service member higher security disclosure and return","requirement":"On or after April 1, 2025, if a landlord or agent charges a service member tenant higher than standard or advertised security due to credit history, credit score, housing history, or other tenant-related factor, the landlord must give a written statement before lease signing of the higher amount and why it is charged; the extra security must be returned after no more than six months of residency if the tenant is not in arrears, with the return date included in the lease.","key_value":{"effective_date":"2025-04-01","return_deadline":"after no more than six months of residency","condition":"tenant not in arrears"},"coverage_conditions":["service member tenant","higher than standard or advertised security","due to credit history, credit score, housing history, or other factor related to tenant"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits","tenant_type":"service member","as_of_date":"2026-10-01"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(4)","quoted_span":"On or after April 1, 2025, if a landlord or its agent charges a service member who rents residential property in which the service member will reside a higher than standard or advertised security pursuant to paragraph (1) due to the credit history, credit score, housing history, or other factor related to the tenant, the landlord shall provide the tenant with a written statement, on or before the date the lease is signed, of the amount of the higher security and an explanation why the higher security amount is being charged.","interaction":"Exception/add-on to (c)(1); “service member” per Military and Veterans Code § 400.","confidence":0.97,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Small landlord two-month security cap","requirement":"Notwithstanding the one-month cap, a landlord shall not demand or receive security exceeding two months' rent, in addition to first month's rent, if the landlord is a natural person or an LLC whose members are all natural persons, and owns no more than two residential rental properties collectively including no more than four dwelling units offered for rent.","key_value":{"max_security":"two months' rent","max_properties":2,"max_units":4},"coverage_conditions":["landlord natural person or LLC all members natural persons","landlord owns no more than two residential rental properties","properties collectively include no more than four dwelling units offered for rent"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits","landlord_type":"natural person or qualifying LLC"},"exemptions":["service member prospective tenant exception under (c)(5)(B)"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(5)(A)","quoted_span":"Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to two months’ rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy if the landlord meets both of the following requirements:","interaction":"Overrides (c)(1) for qualifying small landlords; subject to (c)(5)(B) and (c)(6).","confidence":0.96,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Service member exception and no-refusal rule","requirement":"Subparagraph (A) does not apply if the prospective tenant is a service member. A landlord shall not refuse to enter a residential rental agreement with a prospective service member tenant because this subparagraph prohibits demanding or receiving greater security than the one-month amount in paragraph (1).","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["prospective tenant is a service member"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits","tenant_type":"service member"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(5)(B)","quoted_span":"A landlord shall not refuse to enter into a rental agreement for residential property with a prospective tenant who is a service member because this subparagraph prohibits the landlord from demanding or receiving a greater amount of security than that which is established in paragraph (1).","interaction":"Exception to (c)(5)(A); “service member” per Military and Veterans Code § 400.","confidence":0.96,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Natural person and family trust definitions for small-landlord cap","requirement":"For (c)(5), 'natural person' includes a natural person who is settlor or beneficiary of a family trust; 'family trust' means a revocable living trust or irrevocable trust whose settlors and beneficiaries are related as sibling, spouse, domestic partner, child, parent, grandparent, or grandchild.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["interpretation of (c)(5)"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(5)(C)","quoted_span":"“Natural person” includes any natural person who is a settlor or beneficiary of a family trust.","interaction":"Definition used in (c)(5)(A).","confidence":0.94,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Subdivision (c) does not apply to pre-July 1, 2024 security","requirement":"Subdivision (c) does not apply to security collected or demanded by the landlord before July 1, 2024.","key_value":{"cutoff_date":"2024-07-01"},"coverage_conditions":["security collected or demanded before July 1, 2024"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(c)(6)","quoted_span":"This subdivision shall not apply to a security collected or demanded by the landlord before July 1, 2024.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security held for tenant; tenant priority over creditors","requirement":"Any security must be held by the landlord for the tenant who is party to the lease or agreement. The tenant's claim to the security is prior to any creditor of the landlord.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["security held by landlord"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(d)","quoted_span":"Any security shall be held by the landlord for the tenant who is party to the lease or agreement. The claim of a tenant to the security shall be prior to the claim of any creditor of the landlord.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Claims against security limited to reasonably necessary amounts","requirement":"Subject to paragraph (2), the landlord may claim of the security only amounts reasonably necessary for the purposes specified in subdivision (b).","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["claim against security"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(e)(1)","quoted_span":"Subject to paragraph (2), the landlord may claim of the security only those amounts as are reasonably necessary for the purposes specified in subdivision (b).","interaction":"Read with (b) and (e)(2).","confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No security claims for preexisting conditions or ordinary wear and tear","requirement":"The landlord shall not assert a claim against the tenant or security for damages or defective conditions preexisting the tenancy, for ordinary wear and tear or effects, whether preexisting or during tenancy, or for cumulative effects of ordinary wear and tear during any tenancy.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["damage or defective condition preexisting tenancy","ordinary wear and tear","cumulative effects"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(e)(2)(A)","quoted_span":"The landlord shall not assert a claim against the tenant or the security for damages to the premises or any defective conditions that preexisted the tenancy, for ordinary wear and tear or the effects thereof, whether the wear and tear preexisted the tenancy or occurred during the tenancy, or for the cumulative effects of ordinary wear and tear occurring during any one or more tenancies.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Materials and work claims limited to reasonable restoration","requirement":"Claims against the tenant or security for materials, supplies, and work by a contractor, landlord, or landlord's employee are limited to a reasonable amount necessary to restore the premises to their inception condition, exclusive of ordinary wear and tear.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["claim for materials, supplies, or work"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["ordinary wear and tear"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(e)(2)(B)","quoted_span":"Claims against the tenant or the security for materials or supplies and for work performed by a contractor, the landlord, or the landlord’s employee shall be limited to a reasonable amount necessary to restore the premises back to the condition it was in at the inception of the tenancy, exclusive of ordinary wear and tear.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No professional cleaning charges unless reasonably necessary","requirement":"The landlord shall not require a tenant to pay for, or assert a claim against the tenant or security for, professional carpet cleaning or other professional cleaning services unless reasonably necessary to return the premises to the inception condition, exclusive of ordinary wear and tear.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["professional carpet cleaning or other professional cleaning services"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["reasonably necessary to return premises to inception condition exclusive of ordinary wear and tear"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(e)(2)(C)","quoted_span":"The landlord shall not require a tenant to pay for, or assert a claim against the tenant or the security for, professional carpet cleaning or other professional cleaning services, unless reasonably necessary to return the premises to the condition it was in at the inception of tenancy, exclusive of ordinary wear and tear.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Initial inspection notice and right to be present","requirement":"Within a reasonable time after notice of termination or before end of lease term, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the option to request an initial inspection and the right to be present. Upon request, the landlord or agent must make an initial inspection before final inspection, no earlier than two weeks before termination/end of lease, to let tenant remedy deficiencies.","key_value":{"inspection_timing":"no earlier than two weeks before termination or end of lease date"},"coverage_conditions":["notification of intention to terminate or before end of lease term","tenant requests initial inspection"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["tenant chooses not to request initial inspection","tenancy terminated under CCP § 1161(2),(3),(4)"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(f)(1)","quoted_span":"Within a reasonable time after notification of either party’s intention to terminate the tenancy, or before the end of the lease term, the landlord shall notify the tenant in writing of the tenant’s option to request an initial inspection and of the tenant’s right to be present at the inspection.","interaction":"Inspection requirements subject to (f)(7).","confidence":0.97,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"48-hour inspection notice and waiver","requirement":"The landlord shall give at least 48 hours' prior written notice of the date and time of the inspection if a mutual time is agreed or if no mutual time can be scheduled but tenant still wishes inspection. Tenant and landlord may waive 48-hour notice by both signing a written waiver. Landlord proceeds whether tenant present or not unless tenant withdrew request.","key_value":{"notice_hours":48},"coverage_conditions":["initial inspection requested","mutual time agreed or tenant still wishes inspection"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["written waiver signed by both parties","tenant withdrew request"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(f)(1)","quoted_span":"The landlord shall give at least 48 hours’ prior written notice of the date and time of the inspection","interaction":null,"confidence":0.97,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Itemized statement of proposed deductions after initial inspection","requirement":"Based on the inspection, the landlord shall give the tenant an itemized statement specifying repairs or cleanings proposed as basis for deductions under (b)(1)-(4), and include the texts of those paragraphs. If tenant is present, give to tenant; otherwise leave inside premises.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["initial inspection conducted"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(f)(2)","quoted_span":"Based on the inspection, the landlord shall give the tenant an itemized statement specifying repairs or cleanings that are proposed to be the basis of any deductions from the security the landlord intends to make pursuant to paragraphs (1) to (4), inclusive, of subdivision (b).","interaction":"Read with (b)(1)-(4).","confidence":0.97,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant opportunity to remedy before termination","requirement":"The tenant shall have the opportunity from the initial inspection until termination to remedy identified deficiencies, consistent with the rental agreement, to avoid deductions from security.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["initial inspection identified deficiencies"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(f)(3)","quoted_span":"The tenant shall have the opportunity during the period following the initial inspection until termination of the tenancy to remedy identified deficiencies, in a manner consistent with the rights and obligations of the parties under the rental agreement, in order to avoid deductions from the security.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Limits on deductions after initial inspection","requirement":"If an initial inspection is conducted and no tenant possessions prevent identifying repairs or cleanings, the landlord shall not use security for deductions for repairs or cleanings not identified in the itemized statement. This does not prevent deductions for identified damages not cured or for purposes in (b)(1)-(4) occurring after completion of initial inspection or not identified due to tenant possessions.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["initial inspection conducted","premises do not contain tenant possessions preventing identification"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["deductions itemized and not cured","damages occurring between initial inspection and return of possession","items not identified due to tenant possessions"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(f)(4)-(6)","quoted_span":"the landlord shall not use the security for deductions for repairs or cleanings that are not identified in the itemized statement described in paragraph (2).","interaction":"Read with (f)(2).","confidence":0.96,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Inspection requirements do not apply to certain evictions","requirement":"The requirements of subdivision (f) do not apply when the tenancy is terminated pursuant to subdivision (2), (3), or (4) of Section 1161 of the Code of Civil Procedure.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["tenancy terminated under CCP § 1161(2),(3),(4)"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(f)(7)","quoted_span":"The requirements of this subdivision do not apply when the tenancy is terminated pursuant to subdivision (2), (3), or (4) of Section 1161 of the Code of Civil Procedure.","interaction":"Exception to (f).","confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Photograph unit before tenancy inception","requirement":"For tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025, the landlord shall take photographs of the unit immediately before, or at the inception of, the tenancy.","key_value":{"effective_date":"2025-07-01"},"coverage_conditions":["tenancy begins on or after July 1, 2025"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(g)(1)","quoted_span":"For tenancies that begin on or after July 1, 2025, the landlord shall take photographs of the unit immediately before, or at the inception of, the tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Photograph unit after possession returned and after repairs","requirement":"Beginning April 1, 2025, the landlord shall take photographs within a reasonable time after possession is returned, before repairs or cleanings for which security will be deducted or claimed, and again within a reasonable time after those repairs or cleanings are completed.","key_value":{"effective_date":"2025-04-01"},"coverage_conditions":["possession returned","repairs or cleanings for deduction/claim against security"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(g)(2)","quoted_span":"Beginning April 1, 2025, the landlord shall take photographs of the unit within a reasonable time after the possession of the unit is returned to the landlord, but prior to any repairs or cleanings for which the landlord will make a deduction from or claim against the security deposit pursuant to this section, and shall also take photographs of the unit within a reasonable time after such repairs or cleanings are completed.","interaction":"Read with (h)(2)(D).","confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security return and itemized statement deadline","requirement":"No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant vacates, but not earlier than specified notice/60-day periods, the landlord shall furnish an itemized statement of any security received and the disposition, and return any remaining security to the tenant.","key_value":{"deadline_days":21,"timeframe":"after tenant vacates"},"coverage_conditions":["tenant has vacated premises"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(h)(1)","quoted_span":"No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant has vacated the premises","interaction":"Read with (h)(2)-(7) for documentation and forfeiture.","confidence":0.98,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Methods for returning security and furnishing itemized statement","requirement":"Security remainder must be returned by personal delivery or first-class mail check, except if received electronically then electronically to a designated account or by written agreement. Itemized statement by personal delivery or first-class mail, or by email if mutually agreed. If multiple adult tenants, return check to all adult tenants and furnish statement to one, unless a written mutual agreement specifies allocation/delivery, with special rule for Section 1946.7 termination.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["return of security remainder","furnishing itemized statement","multiple adult tenants if applicable"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["written agreement designating other method","mutual agreement for email","multiple-tenant written agreement","Section 1946.7 termination exception"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(h)(1)(A)-(C)","quoted_span":"the landlord shall return the remainder of the security by personal delivery or by a check made payable to the tenant and mailed by first-class mail, postage prepaid.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Documentation required with itemized statement","requirement":"The landlord shall include copies of documents showing charges incurred and deducted to repair or clean: if landlord/employee did work, describe work, time, and hourly rate; if not, provide bill/invoice/receipt with name, address, phone; for materials/supplies, provide copy of bill/invoice/receipt or vendor document; for repairs/cleanings, provide photographs per (g) and written explanation of allowable cost.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":["deductions for repairs or cleaning"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":["$125 or less deductions","tenant waiver under (h)(4)","tenant request under (h)(5) overrides"],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(h)(2)","quoted_span":"The landlord shall also include, along with and at the same time the itemized statement is sent, copies of documents showing charges incurred and deducted by the landlord to repair or clean the premises, as follows:","interaction":"Read with (g) and (h)(4)-(5).","confidence":0.97,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Good faith estimate for incomplete repairs or missing documents","requirement":"If a repair cannot reasonably be completed within 21 days after vacating, or if provider documents are not in landlord's possession within 21 days, the landlord may deduct a good faith estimate and provide it with the itemized statement, including provider name/address/phone if applicable; within 14 days of completing repair or receiving documentation, landlord must complete (h)(1)-(2) requirements.","key_value":{"repair_docs_deadline_days":21,"complete_requirements_days":14},"coverage_conditions":["repair cannot reasonably be completed within 21 days","documents from provider not in possession within 21 days"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(h)(3)","quoted_span":"If a repair to be done by the landlord or the landlord’s employee cannot reasonably be completed within 21 calendar days after the tenant has vacated the premises, or if the documents from a person or entity providing services, materials, or supplies are not in the landlord’s possession within 21 calendar days after the tenant has vacated the premises, the landlord may deduct the amount of a good faith estimate of the charges that will be incurred and provide that estimate with the itemized statement.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.97,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Documentation exception for small deductions or waiver","requirement":"The landlord need not comply with (h)(2) or (h)(3) if deductions for repairs and cleaning together do not exceed $125, or if the tenant waived those rights in a signed writing at the same time or after a termination notice or no earlier than 60 days before a fixed-term lease expires. The waiver must substantially include the text of paragraph (2).","key_value":{"threshold":"$125"},"coverage_conditions":["deductions for repairs and cleaning together do not exceed $125","or tenant signed waiver meeting timing requirements"],"applicability":{"jurisdiction":"CA","topic":"security_deposits"},"exemptions":[],"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5(h)(4)","quoted_span":"The landlord need not comply with paragraph (2) or (3) if either of the following applies:","interaction":"Subject to (h)(5).","confidence":0.96,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
